EPIC-260715-2mqgvm_viability-and-foundation/STORY-260715-lkshfz_ssh-engine-spike/TASK-260715-2d3g5e_add-common-ssh-transport-conformance-tests/README.md:7:In scope: production libssh2 Tier-1 M0 host-key ordering, approved auth, direct-tcpip, exec/stdin upload, bounded buffers and backpressure, client rekey, server-rekey handling, keepalive, per-site cancellation, lifecycle, privacy-safe errors, available metrics, deterministic resource baselines, and explicit deferred-state assertions; ReluxNIOSSH remains a first-class unavailable/deferred matrix entry. Out of scope: new ReluxNIOSSH adapter or fork work, treating M3 exact values as M0 selection gates, fabricating candidate behavior, production lane scheduling, physical performance, relay framing, UI, and sleep-only tests.
