EPIC-260715-3810we_tcp-dns-system-vpn/STORY-260715-2bfjhn_dns-and-ip-routing/TASK-260721-3miqh4_establish-evidence-gated-dns-runtime-limits/README.md:10:1. A TASK-ID-scoped evidence report compares candidate endpoint cardinalities, message sizes, capacities, byte budgets, and timing values against primary DNS and SSH requirements, accepted runtime memory and startup contracts, and repeatable controlled-fixture measurements. 2. The selected DNSRuntimePolicyV1 names exact injectable production defaults and validation ceilings for endpoint count, maximum DNS message bytes, in-flight queries, queued and aggregate bytes, channel-open, response, logical, startup, and idle timing, and proves every cross-field relationship; no value is stored in the user profile unless ADR-022 requires it. 3. Worst-case accounting reserves request, maximum response, framing, correlation metadata, connection buffers, retry batch, and queued bytes within an explicit DNS component budget; inconsistent policies fail validation and measurements record peak footprint and cleanup. 4. Reliability evidence covers IPv4-only, IPv6-only, dual ordered, loopback, unreachable, malformed, and stalling endpoints, concurrent connection failure, cancellation, and M2 one-UDP-plus-bounded-TCP semantics with no physical resolver access. 5. An independent architecture reviewer accepts the values and revalidation triggers, and the task updates ADR-022, the routing and DNS source of truth, test vectors, and concrete downstream task resources before production composition or profile UX consumes defaults.
