EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-243sh0_ios-testflight-and-app-store/README.md:7:In scope: Apple Distribution and App Store Connect credential ownership, distribution profiles, host and extension identifiers and entitlements, archive and export configuration, relay and compliance-resource embedding, semantic and build version propagation, embedded-profile and entitlement inspection, TestFlight upload and processing, internal tester rollout, physical iPhone installation and VPN lifecycle checks, privacy manifest and export-compliance validation, symbols, App Store binary preflight, source-to-archive provenance, signed-build reproducibility boundaries, and rollback or supersession runbooks. Out of scope: Developer ID and notarization, public App Store marketing or legal copy owned by the review story, product feature implementation, simulator-only acceptance, live production credentials in tests, and claiming byte-identical signed IPAs when Apple signing introduces nondeterminism.
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-243sh0_ios-testflight-and-app-store/README.md:10:1. A clean release archive embeds exactly the approved iOS tunnel extension and required relay or compliance resources, uses matching distribution profiles, and passes automated bundle ID, team, App Group, Keychain, packet-tunnel entitlement, version, and embedded-profile inspection. 2. Protected CI allocates a monotonic build number, exports the declared App Store method, uploads to App Store Connect, waits for processing, records identifiers, and distributes the same candidate to the intended TestFlight group without exposing credentials. 3. A named physical iPhone installs the TestFlight build and passes first launch, privacy and permission gates, extension start and stop, full or degraded capability, app termination, sleep or wake, network change, diagnostics, and uninstall acceptance. 4. The candidate passes App Store validation for architecture, symbols, privacy manifests, required-reason APIs where applicable, export compliance, bundle metadata, and prohibited private APIs. 5. Evidence binds source commit, dependency locks, generator and Xcode versions, relay manifest, protocol version, marketing and build versions, archive and export checksums, profiles, signing identities, and App Store Connect build ID while distinguishing reproducible unsigned inputs from signed outputs. 6. Expiring, withdrawing, superseding, or rejecting a TestFlight build and rotating or revoking credentials follows a tested runbook without corrupting version history or promoting an unverified binary.
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-243sh0_ios-testflight-and-app-store/TASK-260715-3ixjf7_produce-ios-distribution-acceptance-evidence/README.md:4:Perform the independent end-to-end iOS distribution gate and publish a verdict over the exact archive, TestFlight build, physical-device results, privacy and export checks, provenance, App Store preflight, and rollback readiness.
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-243sh0_ios-testflight-and-app-store/TASK-260715-3ixjf7_produce-ios-distribution-acceptance-evidence/README.md:7:In scope: exact source and App Store Connect build ID, archive and export digests, bundle topology, profiles, entitlements, versions, relay integrity, privacy manifests, required-reason APIs, symbols, export record, provenance, TestFlight processing and group, physical matrix, accessibility, lifecycle, diagnostics, withdrawal rehearsal, secret audit, evidence completeness, and pass or fail index. Out of scope: implementing fixes, accepting simulator-only proof, submitting App Review, legal or regional approval, macOS distribution, and overriding an Apple or security failure.
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-243sh0_ios-testflight-and-app-store/TASK-260715-3ixjf7_produce-ios-distribution-acceptance-evidence/README.md:10:1. The auditor independently verifies the candidate identity from source and archived bytes through App Store Connect build ID and named-device TestFlight installation. 2. Exact host and extension profiles, entitlements, versions, architectures, relay resources, privacy manifests, symbols, export answers, and provenance pass without development-only or extra rights. 3. TestFlight processing, intended group distribution, physical lifecycle and accessibility matrix, server preflight, evidence retention, and withdrawal or credential recovery rehearsal all pass or produce a blocking result. 4. Logs, archives, symbols, reports, caches, and evidence contain no private certificate key, issuer key, password, production SSH credential, or user traffic. 5. A TASK-ID-scoped verdict lists every gate, environment, command, artifact digest, build ID, result, anomaly, residual risk, and blocker and is required before App Review submission.
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-2dtdql_release-operations-privacy-and-review/README.md:10:1. A versioned release manifest and runbook identify candidate commits and artifacts, owners, approvals, required CI gates, promotion order, communication, retention, abort criteria, rollback, revocation, and post-release checks for relay, macOS, and iOS. 2. A currently dated primary-source review plus accountable product, privacy, legal, security, and regional approvals produce public policy, App Privacy labels, export-compliance answers, retention or deletion commitments, and storefront availability that match actual behavior. 3. The App Review package accurately explains the VPN data path, Network Extension purpose, user-owned SSH exit, observer boundaries, system exclusions, full and degraded modes, diagnostics, support data, and regional limits without claiming anonymity or a Relux-operated exit service. 4. Reviewers receive a reproducible test profile or isolated SSH host and instructions that exercise the submitted binary without exposing private production credentials; access is scoped, monitored for abuse, rotated, and removed after review. 5. The exact signed candidates pass the supported simulator, physical iPhone, Apple-silicon Mac, accessibility, privacy, leak, lifecycle, entitlement, notarization, TestFlight, artifact, migration, install, upgrade, and rollback matrix, with failures blocking promotion. 6. Submission metadata, screenshots, privacy and support URLs, binary and build identifiers, reviewer notes, communications, rejections, corrections, and resubmissions are preserved and traceable to the reviewed behavior and evidence revision.
